{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Q2WPkEWcFVRiWaHVHr2Fi","type":"tool_result","content":"1108\t\n1109\t      # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n1110\t      # Step: Harness-config gate (PLAN-153 Wave E item 1 / ADR-173)\n1111\t      #\n1112\t      # `.claude/hooks/check_harness_config.py` certifies the hook rail is\n1113\t      # ALIVE, not merely present (the S254 dead-pair-rail class: a\n1114\t      # registered hook whose shim path never resolves fail-opens `{}`\n1115\t      # silently at runtime and no static exec-bit sweep sees it):\n1116\t      #   - static: runtime-resolution model over settings.json hook\n1117\t      #     commands ($CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR-anchored or absolute only; shim\n1118\t      #     args must resolve at the shim's dirname), inline-secret scan,\n1119\t      #     DENY_BASELINE subset check, no-op annotation check, plus\n1120\t      #     delegation to check-active-hooks-executable.py (exec bits —\n1121\t      #     single owner, re-run here so this gate is self-contained).\n1122\t      #   - behavioral: replays planted-violation fixtures\n1123\t      #     (.claude/hooks/_lib/harness_replay/ — inert\n1124\t      #     test data) through the REAL hooks in a hermetic env (temp\n1125\t      #     HOME/GNUPGHOME, no override/sentinel env leakage) and asserts\n1126\t      #     each rail BLOCKS its positive control. A dead rail cannot\n1127\t      #     pass this half.\n1128\t      # No-arg invocation = static + replay, matching the /ceo-boot\n1129\t      # `harness_config_gate` check for CI/boot parity. Local-only: NO\n1130\t      # network, NO credential — safe on fork PRs. CEO_SOTA_DISABLE=1\n1131\t      # skips the replay half in-script (static unaffected); the\n1132\t      # job-level `if:` gate above skips the whole job anyway.\n1133\t      # Exit contract: 0 green / 1 RED finding(s) / 2 unusable input —\n1134\t      # ANY non-zero fails this step (fail-closed gate