{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7AR3PRQQzcaJ12ujFo2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LqasZ7MfVcp8Ve1PusRGUr","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 23/34: .claude/hooks/check_canonical_edit.py (logic moved into .claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/*), .claude/hooks/check_cost_envelope.py, .claude/hooks/check_harness_config.py.\n\nHOW THIS WAS CHECKED\nStatic review only, against the candidate tree. There is no git here, so the base is known only from the removed lines in the payload. I ran no code.\n\nSAME CODE AS THE RC\nThe three diff headers in this payload are identical to those in the committed rc evidence (.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/diff-rc1-22.patch, lines 2, 2613 and 2643):\n- check_canonical_edit.py: d9f5090a2257..ae94653b88aa\n- check_cost_envelope.py: 0f3052a56c21..057d8286d3f7\n- check_harness_config.py: d95dc4f21e18..cc7f27d2785c\nSo the GA blobs of these files are the rc blobs. This fits the GA-only condition that no code changed between the rc and the GA. The rc verdicts on the same content are claude-rc1-22 and codex-rc1-22.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS TOUCHED BY THIS PAYLOAD\n- Condition 5: true. check_arbitration_kernel.py:309 lists \".claude/hooks/_lib/canonical_edit/**/*\", and the hook file itself stays on the list at :94.\n- Condition 7: true. check_canonical_edit.py keeps its path, its __main__ dispatch and the --is-canonical command (:643-651). The logic now lives in _lib/canonical_edit/{guards,paths,sentinels,signature_rail,session_roots,utility,decisions,entry}.py, so a hand-applied patch must be applied again in the module, and that module is a kernel path.\n- GA-only condition (P1 lane notes stay open): the partial-install P1 reproduces unchanged; it is described below as carried, not filed as new.\n- CHANGELOG [1.4.4] lines 324-326, 329-331 and 334-336 match the diff.\n\nMOVED-CODE CHECKS (item 4), all clean\n- Binding. canonical_edit/__init__.py:16-31 rebuilds every exported function with FunctionType(code, the hook's globals, ...). As a result:\n  - The `global` writes (_SENTINEL_CACHE_HITS and _MISSES, _UNLOCK_TRUST_DIAG, _CURRENT_TOOL_NAME) land in the hook module.\n  - Patch points on check_canonical_edit (_gpg_verify, _sentinel_signers, _now, _SENTINEL_SIGNERS_FILE, _verify_signature_rail and others) still reach the moved callers.\n- Name coverage. Every upper-case global the components use is defined in the hook: the constants at :77-605 and the guards re-export at :118-122. The only other such names (_PERSONA_COVERAGE_ARCHETYPES, _LAYER_3A_REASON_CODES, _PATTERNS) appear only in comments or docstrings, or are local variables.\n- File-relative anchors. _SENTINEL_SIGNERS_REGISTRY_YAML and _SENTINEL_SIGNERS_FILE are still computed from the hook's own __file__ (:77-96), so moving the code did not move them.\n- Default arguments. All defaults in the components are literals (None or \"\"), so nothing is evaluated in the component modules, which import nothing.\n- Import order. The guards are bound at :118, before _CANONICAL_GUARDS_FOLDED is computed at :201. No bound function runs at import time.\n- Text. signature_rail.py and sentinels.py:1-140 match the removed text exactly.\n- Shared list. The _CANONICAL_GUARDS list object is now shared across imports, but nothing outside .claude/plans mutates it.\n- Python 3.9 and stdlib. No 3.10+ syntax, only standard-library imports.\n\nP0: none.\n\nCARRIED P1s (already declared through the signed rc lane notes; re-confirmed here, not new)\n1. P1, check_canonical_edit.py:118-127 and :616-640 (same logic at _lib/canonical_edit/entry.py:126-134). Raised by claude-p22, codex-p22 and codex-p17.\n   (a) Any component module missing (ImportError): the fallback main() prints {\"decision\":\"block\"} for every Edit, Write, MultiEdit and mcp__ event without reading the event, including non-canonical files and read-only MCP tools. That is an infrastructure fault failing CLOSED, against item 2. It also prints Claude-shaped JSON whatever the adapter is.\n   (b) Only guards.py missing or failing: :123-127 sets _CANONICAL_GUARDS = [] but leaves _COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR unset. bind() still succeeds, because __init__ does not import guards. Then:\n     - every canonical path is classified non-canonical and the edit is allowed, with no breadcrumb;\n     - --is-canonical prints 0 for every path and exits 0;\n     - an mcp__ event raises NameError on _MCP_WRITE_PATH_KEYS, exits 1, and is allowed.\n   Precondition: a partial or corrupted install. Normal install and upgrade deliver the whole package, and the kernel hard-deny still covers kernel paths on its own, so this stays P1.\n   Minimal fix:\n     - send a guards import failure into the _COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR state;\n     - make the CLI exit nonzero in that state;\n     - block only candidates whose first path segment is in _CANONICAL_PREFIXES_FOLDED, allow the rest with a breadcrumb, and emit through the resolved adapter.\n2. P1, _lib/_ceo_boot_parts/harness_governance.py:300-325 (raised by claude-p06 as P1-a). It parses check_canonical_edit.py looking for an `_PATTERNS =` assignment, which now lives in _lib/canonical_edit/paths.py, so it always falls back. Re-confirmed against this facade.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): no undeclared P1 in this payload.\n\nOTHER FILES (checked, no defect beyond P2 1)\n- check_cost_envelope.py:182-187 and :248-252.\n  - With CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR unset or relative, or runtime_paths missing, the hook writes a breadcrumb, returns {} and records no spend. That fails open on missing scope, as the CHANGELOG states, and it no longer writes a ledger under whatever the current directory is.\n  - The hook is registered only in this repo's own .claude/settings.json:318, not in templates/settings/*, and its command line already expands $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR. Adopter impact is nil.\n- check_harness_config.py:583-606 (exec-bit sub-check).\n  - An exception in the delegated 